# rule.forbid.sync-invoke-while-a-pty-is-live

> **while a test holds a live background pty, it never calls a child process synchronously.
> use `invokeRhachetCliBinaryAsync`, never `invokeRhachetCliBinary` (`spawnSync`).**

## .why — a sync call starves the pty it alone drains

`spawnRhachetCliBackground` reads its pty through `child.onData`, which fires only while the test's
event loop turns. a `spawnSync` freezes that loop. the clone's tui writes without pause, the kernel pty
buffer fills, the clone blocks inside its own sync tty write, and so cannot serve its socket — a
`clone say` gets no `delivered` ack, waits out its 30s wedge, and exits **2**. then the loop resumes,
the pty drains, and the clone delivers the message it held.

⇒ **a deadlock the test made, which reads as a product wedge**: `said.status = 2`, yet `landed = true`.
🔴 it is load-dependent — solo runs pass; a full parallel suite fills the buffer first.

🟡 only a call that needs the clone's loop (`clone say`) can deadlock; `clone list`/`get` only delay
the drain. use the async twin for both — the rule is cheaper to hold than the distinction.

measured 2026-09-25, `clone.joker.realbrain` [t4]: exit 2 after 34.5s (the 30s wedge plus a reply).
on the async twin: 19/19 in 30s solo, 27/27 across the three real-brain suites.

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| a test holds a `spawnRhachetCliBackground` handle | every child call in its scope is async |
| a say exits 2 but its reply lands moments later | 🔴 suspect this rule before the product |
| a real-brain flake appears only under the full suite | suspect a starved pty before a slow brain |
| you add a helper that invokes the cli beside a live pty | it takes the async twin, never the sync one |

scope: blackbox tests and infra that spawn a background pty. a test with no live pty may stay sync.

blocker: a `clone say` via `spawnSync` while a background pty is live.
nitpick: any other sync child call while a background pty is live.

⇒ see also: `invokeRhachetCliBinary.ts` (the async twin) · `enrollCloneHarness.ts`
(`sayAndPollForMarker`) · `define.invariant.clone-say-delivery`.
